        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement Asean China Diplomacy China backs Myanmar’s push to ease diplomatic isolation, stamp out telecoms scams Foreign Minister Wang Yi caps five-day Southeast Asia tour also urging both sides to ‘open up new prospects for bilateral relations’ 2 -MIN READ 2 -MIN Listen Vanessa Cai in Shanghai Published: 6:37pm, 26 Apr 2026 China has pledged to help Myanmar ’s new government to engage more with multilateral platforms and eradicate telecoms scam operations. Capping a five-day trip to Southeast Asia on the weekend, Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi told Min Aung Hlaing, Myanmar’s junta leader-turned-president , on Saturday that China “firmly supports Myanmar in safeguarding its national sovereignty, security and territorial integrity”. “This year marks the first year of Myanmar’s new government. Both sides should seize this opportunity to carry forward their traditional friendship and open up new prospects for bilateral relations,” Wang said in the capital city Naypyidaw, according to a Chinese foreign ministry statement. Advertisement Min Aung Hlaing was sworn in as president earlier this month after Myanmar’s military-dominated legislature elected him as president on April 3. Myanmar has been engulfed in civil war since February 2021 , when the military overthrew the elected government of Aung San Suu Kyi and detained its leaders. 01:32 Myanmar frees Win Myint, cuts Aung San Suu Kyi’s prison term in broad-ranging amnesty deal Myanmar frees Win Myint, cuts Aung San Suu Kyi’s prison term in broad-ranging amnesty deal Wang said China was willing to maintain and strengthen strategic coordination. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
